OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AHow the downfall of Serbia's VuDMiDK
OL,4,Amirrored that of Hungary's Orban
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Tisza party in Hungary and the
OL,7,FStudent List in Serbia look very
OL,8,Fdifferent - Tisza is centred on the
OL,9,Fpersonality and energy of its leader,
OL,10,Fwhile the students in Serbia insist
OL,11,Fthey have no leadership.
OL,13,FBut the huge turnout - 79% in Hungary
OL,14,Fand 69% in Serbia, was driven by
OL,15,Ftech-savvy young people in both
OL,16,Fcountries. They used AI tools to crunch
OL,17,Fnumbers, identify threats to the vote,
OL,18,Fand mobilise tens of thousands of
OL,19,Felection monitors to prevent
OL,20,Fintimidation and electoral fraud by the
OL,21,Fgoverning parties.
OL,23,APub: 01-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
